---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { Badge } from '@highjack/ui';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Rules — HighJack"
  description="How HighJack rules work: a configurable ruleset, validation of impossible combinations, and three ways to win."
>
  <header class="max-w-3xl">
    <h1 class="m-0 font-display text-3xl font-extrabold sm:text-4xl">How the rules work</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 mb-0 text-lg leading-relaxed text-muted-400">
      A match is defined by its <strong class="text-cream-100">GameConfig</strong>. The engine
      enforces exactly what that document says, and rejects combinations that cannot work.
    </p>
  </header>

  <section class="mt-12" aria-labelledby="principles-title">
    <h2 id="principles-title" class="m-0 font-display text-2xl font-extrabold">Principles</h2>
    <div class="mt-6 grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2">
      <article class="rounded-lg border border-line-subtle bg-surface-raised p-6 shadow-card">
        <h3 class="m-0 font-display text-lg font-bold text-gold-400">Only what the config allows</h3>
        <p class="mb-0 mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-400">
          A rule that is not enabled does not exist at that table. Turn off the passing-go bonus and
          nobody collects it. The engine, not the browser, decides what is legal.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="rounded-lg border border-line-subtle bg-surface-raised p-6 shadow-card">
        <h3 class="m-0 font-display text-lg font-bold text-gold-400">Impossible rules are rejected</h3>
        <p class="mb-0 mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-400">
          Validation runs in layers. Malformed documents are refused outright, structural mistakes
          are reported field by field, and impossible combinations never reach a match.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="rounded-lg border border-line-subtle bg-surface-raised p-6 shadow-card">
        <h3 class="m-0 font-display text-lg font-bold text-gold-400">Money is exact</h3>
        <p class="mb-0 mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-400">
          Chips are integers. There are no fractions, so the arithmetic matches on every client and
          on the server.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="rounded-lg border border-line-subtle bg-surface-raised p-6 shadow-card">
        <h3 class="m-0 font-display text-lg font-bold text-gold-400">Rolls are seeded</h3>
        <p class="mb-0 mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-400">
          Dice come from a stream derived from the match seed. The same seed and the same actions
          reproduce the same match, so any result can be checked afterwards.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-12" aria-labelledby="victory-title">
    <h2 id="victory-title" class="m-0 font-display text-2xl font-extrabold">Victory conditions</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 mb-5 max-w-3xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-400">
      Every configuration picks exactly one way to win.
    </p>
    <div class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-3">
      <article class="rounded-lg border border-line-subtle bg-surface-raised p-5 text-center shadow-card">
        <Badge tone="gold">last_standing</Badge>
        <p class="mb-0 mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-400">
          Outlive everyone. Bankruptcies thin the table until one player remains.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="rounded-lg border border-line-subtle bg-surface-raised p-5 text-center shadow-card">
        <Badge tone="gold">target_wealth</Badge>
        <p class="mb-0 mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-400">
          Be the first to reach the chip target set for the match.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="rounded-lg border border-line-subtle bg-surface-raised p-5 text-center shadow-card">
        <Badge tone="gold">round_limit</Badge>
        <p class="mb-0 mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-400">
          When the round limit is reached, the player with the most chips wins.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section
    class="mt-12 rounded-lg border border-line-subtle bg-felt-900/60 p-6"
    aria-label="Rulebook status"
  >
    <h2 class="m-0 font-display text-lg font-bold text-cream-100">The engine is the rulebook</h2>
    <p class="mb-0 mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-400">
      The playable turn and property rules live in the engine source. The configuration schema is
      shared with the client so both sides validate the same document. Nothing is described here
      that the engine does not enforce.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
